findings.detail:
renderRuns derives its three counters purely from `run.members` (u11-widgets.js:574-577: `var members = run.members || []`, then running/queued/done filters). run:plan-12 has no `members` array at all — u11-data.js:864-878 gives it `routePlan` instead — so all three counters resolve to 0 and are rendered as literal zeros at :581-585. Contradicted on the same page by:
- the Completion capacity widget: "Spec: U11 usage concept / PLANNING RUN / Requested 6 / Can run now 2 / Queued 4";
- the run-detail panel: "6 required specialists / 2 admitted now · effective concurrency 2 / 4 queued · 3 waves" and "ACTIVITY / 7 ATTEMPTS";
- the Ledger, which groups 7 attempts (ue-570, ue-571, ue-572, ue-573, ue-574, ue-606, ue-607) under work-8, whose runId is run:plan-12.
UF-085 negative constraint: "Do not display missing, disabled, unsupported, blocked, stale, or unknown cost/quota as zero." The absence of a members array is rendered as three zeros rather than unknown/not-exposed, and the zeros deny attribution to work the same dataset attributes elsewhere.
